  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Removed the post-filter push of `w0` and `w1` in `revolve::lattice` (`crates/motion/src/turning/revolve.rs`). Every in-domain band endpoint is already in `lat`. Removing those four lines keeps `lat` strictly inside `[d_lo, d_hi]`. Free air past an end face no longer creates intervals where the scan reads `E(s) = 0` as rest.\n- Computed `k_hi` in `thread_planned_in` (`crates/motion/src/turning/thread.rs`) from the unclamped `f.station_of(p.top_z)`. Kept `s_lo..=s_hi` clamped to `[d_lo, d_hi]` for `ref_top`, valley phase discovery, and the empty-window refusal. A threading pass can now start in free air in front of the end face.\n- Added `crates/motion/tests/turning_thread_end_face.rs` with four pinning tests.\n- Added `docs/decisions/2879-thread-free-air-start.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nTwo defects prevented a free-end thread from starting in front of the end face:\n\n1. `revolve::lattice` filtered `lat` to `[d_lo, d_hi]` and then pushed `w0` and `w1` back into `lat`. Whenever a move band extended past `d_hi` (by 0.1 mm on a free-end groove, or by whole pitches on a free-air lead-in), `revolve::scan` evaluated an air interval where `E(s) = 0` and reported the capped wave floor (5.0 mm) as rest.\n2. `blade::setup` clamped `s_hi` to `d_hi`, and `thread_planned_in` used that clamped `s_hi` in `k_hi`. Setting `top_z` in front of the end face (such as Z81 for a Z78 end face) still started each pass inside the bar at Z77.5.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `crates/motion/tests/turning_thread_end_face.rs`:\n\n- `free_end_groove_band_past_end_face_is_not_rest`: red before fix (`rest_mm: 5.000000000000001`), green after fix.\n- `free_air_lead_in_starts_in_front_of_end_face_and_judges_clean`: red before fix (started at `77.5` instead of `80.5`), green after fix.\n- `free_air_start_still_convicts_real_gouge_and_real_rest_on_part`: checks overcut, shallow cut, missed turn, and a free-air lattice point whose flank clips a solid end face.\n- `groove_at_free_end_face_spilling_into_end_air_is_not_rest`: red before fix (`rest_mm: 4.0`), green after fix.\n\nMutation checks on `turning_thread_end_face`:\n\n- Reverted `crates/motion/src/turning/revolve.rs` to `upstream/main`: red (3 of 4 failed with `rest_mm: 5.0` and `rest_mm: 4.0`). Restored: green.\n- Reverted `crates/motion/src/turning/thread.rs` to `upstream/main`: red (`free_air_lead_in_starts_in_front_of_end_face_and_judges_clean` failed: `got 77.5`). Restored: green.\n\nGates:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (10 steps, 0 failed: `motion build`, `lib`, `turning_blade`, `turning_coarse`, `turning_stock`, `turning_thread`, `turning_thread_cycle`, `turning_thread_dips`, `turning_thread_end_face`, `turning_thread_infeed`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No app-level end-to-end Fanuc G76 post run (tracked in #2878).\n- No UI test or physical machine run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR touches `crates/motion/src/turning/revolve.rs`, `crates/motion/src/turning/thread.rs`, or `crates/motion/tests/turning_thread_end_face.rs`.\n\nChangelog: Turning: threading passes can now start in free air in front of the part end face without the meridian verdict flagging free air as rest.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2879\n",
